**Key idea.** The subtree rooted at $v$ has $\text{size}(v)=1+\text{size}(\text{left})+\text{size}(\text{right})$. A single postorder traversal computes every subtree size bottom-up with $O(1)$ work per node, and we count the nodes whose size is exactly 4.

```c
int count = 0;
int size(struct node *v) {
    if (v == NULL) return 0;
    int s = 1 + size(v->left) + size(v->right);
    if (s == 4) count++;
    return s;
}
```

Each node is visited once, so the time is $O(n)$. Linear time is also needed in general, since any node might be the root of such a subtree.

So $O(n^a\log^b n)=O(n^1\log^0 n)$, giving $a=1$ and $b=0$:
$$a+10b=1+0=1.$$

**Answer: 1**

